Phase 3 / Tasks 1+2: Introduce DIRECT_DATABASE_URL + verify migrations

Changes:
- packages/db/drizzle.config.ts: prefer DIRECT_DATABASE_URL, fall back to
  DATABASE_URL with console.warn so existing deploys keep working.
- packages/db/src/seed/codecamp-seed.ts: dedicated postgres-js client built
  from DIRECT_DATABASE_URL (fallback + warning), uses the now-pool-aware
  buildPostgresOptions for consistency, properly ends client on exit.
- packages/db/src/seed/codecamp-seed.ts: guard top-level seed() under
  'is main module?' check using import.meta.url === file://argv[1].
  Eliminates pre-existing bug where unit tests importing
  findStaleModuleSlugs silently invoked the seed.
- apps/{codecamp,reading,primary,science}-advantage/.env.example: document
  the DATABASE_URL (pooled, 6432) / DIRECT_DATABASE_URL (direct, 5432)
  split. Add commented DATABASE_POOL_MAX tuning hint.

Why:
- FR-3 requires migrations + LISTEN/NOTIFY consumers run on a session-mode
  connection. The codecamp seed wraps many writes in a single transaction
  which would also be safer on a session.
- Backward-compatible fallback prevents breaking any deploy that has not yet
  added the new secret (especially cloudbuild.yaml).

Verification:
- Fresh DB migrate via DIRECT_DATABASE_URL: 68 tables, 17 migration rows.
- Fresh DB seed via DIRECT_DATABASE_URL: 18 modules, 85 lessons.
- db lint + check-types clean. 232/232 unit tests pass.
- 'Seeding codecamp curriculum...' stdout no longer leaks into unit-test
  output (proving the main-module guard works).

Production note (in plan.md): cloudbuild.yaml deliberately NOT updated.
There is no PgBouncer in production yet, so DATABASE_URL == direct
connection already. The fallback path keeps prod working; the operator adds
the DIRECT_DATABASE_URL secret when PgBouncer lands.

